// Title: Suspicious CodePage Switch Via CHCP
// Sigma ID: c7942406-33dd-4377-a564-0f62db0593a3
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-14 | Modified: 2023-03-07
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036
// Description: Detects a code page switch in command line or batch scripts to a rare language
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity (adjust code pages according to your organization's region)
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/intl/code-page-identifiers
//   - https://twitter.com/cglyer/status/1183756892952248325
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_chcp_codepage_switch.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\chcp.com" and (ProcessCommandLine endswith " 936" or ProcessCommandLine endswith " 1258")
